1
00:00:19,560 --> 00:00:20,080
What?

2
00:00:20,320 --> 00:00:21,120
A month?

3
00:00:22,200 --> 00:00:23,680
We still have so many songs to rehearse.

4
00:00:23,680 --> 00:00:25,000
How can we finish them all?

5
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:27,130
We still have many songs left to write.

6
00:00:27,320 --> 00:00:29,040
And the choreography isn't finished either.

7
00:00:29,040 --> 00:00:29,640
Director,

8
00:00:30,120 --> 00:00:31,980
I will follow your arrangements.

9
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:34,530
One month really isn't enough.

10
00:00:35,800 --> 00:00:36,720
Ms. Shen

11
00:00:38,320 --> 00:00:40,440
has a unique eye,

12
00:00:40,440 --> 00:00:41,720
a sharp mind,

13
00:00:42,840 --> 00:00:44,480
but little patience.

14
00:00:45,320 --> 00:00:46,160
So,

15
00:00:46,560 --> 00:00:49,080
we must do everything we can

16
00:00:49,360 --> 00:00:50,840
to catch her attention.

17
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:51,800
Otherwise,

18
00:00:52,200 --> 00:00:52,920
the money

19
00:00:53,760 --> 00:00:55,820
will end up in someone else's pocket.

20
00:00:58,080 --> 00:00:59,640
If we only have a month,

21
00:01:01,680 --> 00:01:04,319
I'll choreograph Grandma's dance first.

22
00:01:04,879 --> 00:01:05,610
You can do it.

23
00:01:06,680 --> 00:01:08,440
I believe in you.

24
00:01:10,480 --> 00:01:12,280
Train an army for a thousand days

25
00:01:12,480 --> 00:01:14,080
to use it for a single moment.

26
00:01:14,880 --> 00:01:16,320
What does 'a moment' mean?

27
00:01:16,320 --> 00:01:18,160
It means,

28
00:01:18,160 --> 00:01:19,200
that was then,

29
00:01:19,960 --> 00:01:21,039
and this is now.

30
00:01:22,720 --> 00:01:23,280
Anyway,

31
00:01:23,840 --> 00:01:24,600
Join me

32
00:01:24,880 --> 00:01:25,940
and chant a slogan.

33
00:01:26,120 --> 00:01:27,440
Go, go, I'm the strongest!

34
00:01:27,440 --> 00:01:29,000
Go, go, I'm the best!

35
00:01:31,280 --> 00:01:33,720
Let's work hard

36
00:01:34,240 --> 00:01:35,759
and strive together.

37
00:01:36,080 --> 00:01:36,720
Together.

38
00:01:38,280 --> 00:01:39,410
I'll leave it to you.

39
00:01:40,720 --> 00:01:42,720
You just dumped this whole thing on me.

40
00:01:42,720 --> 00:01:43,320
What else?

41
00:01:44,440 --> 00:01:45,640
Isn't this your job?

42
00:01:51,479 --> 00:01:52,960
There's simply no time.

43
00:01:55,640 --> 00:01:57,170
Think about it for a second.

44
00:04:07,640 --> 00:04:09,120
Put the scarf on your head.

45
00:04:10,880 --> 00:04:17,600
One, two, three, four, five, six, seven, eight.

46
00:04:17,600 --> 00:04:18,040
Down.

47
00:04:18,279 --> 00:04:20,959
Two, two, three, four.

48
00:04:20,959 --> 00:04:21,320
Up.

49
00:04:21,320 --> 00:04:24,880
Five, six, seven, eight.

50
00:04:26,160 --> 00:04:26,620
Come on.

51
00:04:27,840 --> 00:04:28,840
Let's do it again.

52
00:04:30,600 --> 00:04:34,159
Five, six, seven, eight.

53
00:04:34,280 --> 00:04:41,680
One, two, three, four, five, six, seven, eight.

54
00:04:41,680 --> 00:04:42,159
Down.

55
00:04:42,159 --> 00:04:47,480
Two, two, three, four, five, six.

56
00:04:48,640 --> 00:04:49,360
Stop.

57
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:52,600
Everyone.

58
00:04:53,640 --> 00:04:55,080
We are living people.

59
00:04:55,800 --> 00:04:57,040
Is this dancing?

60
00:04:57,600 --> 00:04:58,840
Or are zombies hitting the street?

61
00:04:58,840 --> 00:04:59,440
Everyone.

62
00:05:00,400 --> 00:05:01,320
Let's do it again.

63
00:05:01,320 --> 00:05:02,440
Qingsong.

64
00:05:03,720 --> 00:05:05,720
That's easy for you to say.

65
00:05:07,320 --> 00:05:09,320
All you do is stand there and give orders.

66
00:05:09,320 --> 00:05:11,320
We've been dancing from day to night

67
00:05:11,720 --> 00:05:13,160
without a drop of water.

68
00:05:13,440 --> 00:05:14,880
My voice is this hoarse.

69
00:05:15,320 --> 00:05:16,560
Did I drink water?

70
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:17,800
Did I eat?

71
00:05:18,560 --> 00:05:19,600
Did I rest?

72
00:05:20,240 --> 00:05:20,720
Tell me,

73
00:05:20,720 --> 00:05:21,720
if we can't complete the audition,

74
00:05:21,720 --> 00:05:23,080
who will take the responsibility?

75
00:05:23,080 --> 00:05:23,810
I don't care.

76
00:05:24,400 --> 00:05:25,280
I'm not practicing anymore.

77
00:05:25,280 --> 00:05:25,600
You!

78
00:05:25,760 --> 00:05:26,490
Meng Tejiao.

79
00:05:27,560 --> 00:05:28,290
Meng Tejiao!

80
00:05:29,320 --> 00:05:30,250
What do you mean?

81
00:05:30,560 --> 00:05:31,560
What do I mean?

82
00:05:32,200 --> 00:05:33,560
All you do is stand there and give orders.

83
00:05:33,560 --> 00:05:35,720
If you're so capable, dance this stupid dance ten times,

84
00:05:35,720 --> 00:05:36,400
or twenty times!

85
00:05:36,400 --> 00:05:37,330
What did you say?

86
00:05:37,880 --> 00:05:39,340
What did you call my dance?

87
00:05:41,320 --> 00:05:42,120
Stupid dance.

88
00:05:42,280 --> 00:05:43,320
Stupid dance!

89
00:05:43,600 --> 00:05:44,880
Then you're a terrible person.

90
00:05:44,880 --> 00:05:46,680
Say it again if you have the guts.

91
00:05:50,080 --> 00:05:50,880
Stupid dance.

92
00:05:50,920 --> 00:05:51,720
Stupid dance.

93
00:05:51,840 --> 00:05:52,760
Stupid dance!

94
00:05:59,120 --> 00:06:00,320
You hit me?

95
00:06:01,600 --> 00:06:04,530
You should look at the master before beating his dog.

96
00:06:05,560 --> 00:06:06,120
Director!

97
00:06:06,120 --> 00:06:06,640
Director,

98
00:06:06,640 --> 00:06:07,280
we have a problem!

99
00:06:07,280 --> 00:06:07,640
What's wrong?

100
00:06:07,640 --> 00:06:07,840
Bad news!

101
00:06:07,840 --> 00:06:08,440
Director,

102
00:06:08,560 --> 00:06:10,290
something terrible happened!

103
00:06:11,400 --> 00:06:13,000
He said my choreography is trash.

104
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:13,560
Is it?

105
00:06:13,880 --> 00:06:15,000
I've lost my voice.

106
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:15,720
I'm not in a hurry.

107
00:06:15,720 --> 00:06:17,240
We've been rehearsing from morning till afternoon.

108
00:06:17,240 --> 00:06:18,320
Don't we get a break?

109
00:06:18,320 --> 00:06:18,560
I...

110
00:06:18,560 --> 00:06:20,080
Meng Tejiao, I'm telling you.

111
00:06:20,080 --> 00:06:21,400
If you apologize right now,

112
00:06:21,400 --> 00:06:23,000
I'll let bygones be bygones.

113
00:06:24,080 --> 00:06:25,010
Watch your tone.

114
00:06:25,440 --> 00:06:26,840
I'm sorry, Mr. Qingsong,

115
00:06:28,120 --> 00:06:30,720
but I can't rehearse this trash dance of yours.

116
00:06:31,640 --> 00:06:32,500
Say that again!

117
00:06:36,480 --> 00:06:37,280
Calm down!

118
00:06:38,600 --> 00:06:39,520
Stop fighting!

119
00:06:42,560 --> 00:06:43,640
Calm down!

120
00:06:49,040 --> 00:06:49,880
Qingsong,

121
00:06:49,880 --> 00:06:50,610
Meng Tejiao!

122
00:06:50,880 --> 00:06:51,560
Come here.

123
00:06:52,840 --> 00:06:53,640
Stop arguing!

124
00:06:53,640 --> 00:06:54,440
Quiet!

125
00:06:55,320 --> 00:06:57,800
I heard you two started this.

126
00:06:57,800 --> 00:06:58,530
Is that true?

127
00:06:58,800 --> 00:07:00,730
Can someone tell me what happened?

128
00:07:01,080 --> 00:07:02,440
Meng Tejiao is a jerk.

129
00:07:02,440 --> 00:07:03,320
One at a time.

130
00:07:08,080 --> 00:07:09,120
Qingsong, you go first.

131
00:07:09,120 --> 00:07:10,640
Meng Tejiao said my choreography is trash.

132
00:07:10,640 --> 00:07:12,040
You know that, Director?

133
00:07:12,800 --> 00:07:13,400
Your turn.

134
00:07:13,720 --> 00:07:15,180
Qingsong called me a jerk.

135
00:07:16,480 --> 00:07:17,240
Okay, I get it.

136
00:07:17,240 --> 00:07:18,800
He insulted my Jiaojiao first.

137
00:07:18,800 --> 00:07:20,730
You two need to calm down right now.

138
00:07:21,240 --> 00:07:23,160
Think about what you just said.

139
00:07:23,720 --> 00:07:24,450
Meng Tejiao,

140
00:07:25,400 --> 00:07:28,320
do you really think Qingsong's choreography is trash?

141
00:07:28,320 --> 00:07:29,120
No.

142
00:07:30,040 --> 00:07:32,680
Qingsong's previous choreographies were all great.

143
00:07:32,680 --> 00:07:34,080
It's just that we were too tired today.

144
00:07:34,080 --> 00:07:35,210
I spoke out of anger.

145
00:07:36,720 --> 00:07:37,120
What about you,

146
00:07:37,120 --> 00:07:37,720
Qingsong?

147
00:07:38,680 --> 00:07:40,940
Do you really think Meng Tejiao is a jerk?

148
00:07:41,880 --> 00:07:42,360
No.

149
00:07:43,720 --> 00:07:44,920
How could he be a jerk?

150
00:07:45,920 --> 00:07:46,920
We get along

151
00:07:47,480 --> 00:07:48,140
quite well.

152
00:07:51,880 --> 00:07:52,760
Now that you two

153
00:07:52,760 --> 00:07:54,040
have calmed down,

154
00:07:54,920 --> 00:07:56,920
you should apologize to each other.

155
00:07:58,840 --> 00:07:59,500
Apologize.

156
00:08:00,160 --> 00:08:01,000
Okay.

157
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:01,680
I will.

158
00:08:02,880 --> 00:08:04,080
I'm sorry, Qingsong.

159
00:08:05,120 --> 00:08:05,850
Meng Tejiao,

160
00:08:06,800 --> 00:08:07,400
I'm sorry.

161
00:08:08,080 --> 00:08:09,610
Shake hands and make peace.

162
00:08:12,480 --> 00:08:13,680
Can we move past this?

163
00:08:14,880 --> 00:08:15,920
Ouch.

164
00:08:17,560 --> 00:08:18,240
Baby.

165
00:08:19,320 --> 00:08:19,960
Be careful.

166
00:08:19,960 --> 00:08:20,880
We've all been together,

167
00:08:20,880 --> 00:08:22,280
rehearsing for so long.

168
00:08:22,280 --> 00:08:23,740
Why did this still happen?

169
00:08:25,120 --> 00:08:25,720
Director.

170
00:08:26,880 --> 00:08:28,600
Usually, we give all our drive,

171
00:08:28,600 --> 00:08:29,640
all our passion,

172
00:08:29,640 --> 00:08:32,000
and all our energy to this rehearsal room,

173
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:33,929
because we're facing an audience.

174
00:08:34,600 --> 00:08:36,400
Now we only have one audience member,

175
00:08:36,400 --> 00:08:37,120
and we don't even know

176
00:08:37,120 --> 00:08:38,650
if they like our play or not.

177
00:08:38,720 --> 00:08:39,919
Where do we get the drive?

178
00:08:39,919 --> 00:08:41,450
Where do we get the passion?

179
00:08:43,200 --> 00:08:44,560
Do you all think so?

180
00:08:44,960 --> 00:08:46,840
Yes.

181
00:08:51,200 --> 00:08:51,960
Otherwise.

182
00:08:52,320 --> 00:08:53,040
This money

183
00:08:53,880 --> 00:08:55,080
will go into someone else's pocket.

184
00:08:55,080 --> 00:08:56,240
One month is really not enough.

185
00:08:56,240 --> 00:08:58,120
I believe in you.

186
00:09:17,720 --> 00:09:18,280
Jinzi.

187
00:09:20,160 --> 00:09:20,720
Jinzi.

188
00:09:22,560 --> 00:09:23,080
Jinzi.

189
00:09:26,240 --> 00:09:27,100
Come on, Jinzi.

190
00:09:27,760 --> 00:09:28,690
Time for dinner.

191
00:09:29,280 --> 00:09:29,960
Come here,

192
00:09:30,320 --> 00:09:31,320
little princess.

193
00:09:38,040 --> 00:09:38,680
Jinzi.

194
00:09:40,240 --> 00:09:42,300
You know Mom has been very busy lately

195
00:09:42,680 --> 00:09:44,340
and has no time to cook for you,

196
00:09:44,440 --> 00:09:46,770
but you can't be too picky about your food.

197
00:09:48,640 --> 00:09:49,100
Come on,

198
00:09:49,280 --> 00:09:49,920
try some.

199
00:09:52,080 --> 00:09:53,880
You're not eating a single bite?

200
00:09:58,440 --> 00:09:59,480
Jinzi,

201
00:10:00,080 --> 00:10:02,010
don't you have any appetite at all?

202
00:10:09,920 --> 00:10:11,240
Jinzi's body temperature is slightly high.

203
00:10:11,240 --> 00:10:12,920
The blood test shows no abnormalities.

204
00:10:12,920 --> 00:10:13,680
For the specifics,

205
00:10:13,680 --> 00:10:15,320
we'll have to wait until we're on duty tomorrow day

206
00:10:15,320 --> 00:10:16,980
to give it a detailed checkup.

207
00:10:17,440 --> 00:10:18,900
We'll give it an IV drip now

208
00:10:19,240 --> 00:10:20,500
to restore its energy.

209
00:10:20,880 --> 00:10:23,680
Then what's the earliest time we can start the checkup?

210
00:10:23,680 --> 00:10:24,360
8:00 a.m.

211
00:10:25,800 --> 00:10:27,060
I'll wait here with it.

212
00:10:42,800 --> 00:10:44,320
The director is never late.

213
00:10:44,320 --> 00:10:45,560
Why isn't she here yet?

214
00:10:45,560 --> 00:10:47,880
Didn't they say we're rehearsing Grandma's song today?

215
00:10:47,880 --> 00:10:48,810
Where is my song?

216
00:10:48,960 --> 00:10:51,880
It seems the director hasn't finished writing it yet.

217
00:10:51,880 --> 00:10:53,210
The song isn't written?

218
00:10:54,480 --> 00:10:55,560
Then how do we rehearse?

219
00:10:55,560 --> 00:10:58,360
Exactly, what are we rehearsing?

220
00:11:01,200 --> 00:11:01,920
Sorry, everyone.

221
00:11:01,920 --> 00:11:02,720
I'm late.

222
00:11:02,920 --> 00:11:04,080
Director.

223
00:11:04,080 --> 00:11:05,680
Is Grandma's song finished?

224
00:11:06,320 --> 00:11:07,180
It's finished.

225
00:11:07,280 --> 00:11:09,010
We can start rehearsing today.

226
00:11:09,200 --> 00:11:10,800
Give this score to Qingsong.

227
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:12,600
Director.

228
00:11:13,080 --> 00:11:15,540
Didn't Mr. Qingsong pull a muscle in his leg?

229
00:11:15,840 --> 00:11:16,560
For the past few days,

230
00:11:16,560 --> 00:11:18,680
Mr. Heying has been leading the rehearsal.

231
00:11:18,680 --> 00:11:19,080
Sorry.

232
00:11:19,280 --> 00:11:21,010
I'm so tired that I'm confused.

233
00:11:21,440 --> 00:11:23,640
I'll go persuade him to come back later.

234
00:11:24,720 --> 00:11:25,680
Let's start now.

235
00:11:26,600 --> 00:11:27,060
Come on.

236
00:11:27,560 --> 00:11:28,240
Take a seat first.

237
00:11:28,240 --> 00:11:30,000
Ning Jin writes songs...

238
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:31,460
It's quite professional.

239
00:11:32,120 --> 00:11:32,850
Let's begin.

240
00:11:36,880 --> 00:11:37,560
How is it?

241
00:12:13,720 --> 00:12:14,840
Does it sound good?

242
00:12:15,080 --> 00:12:16,340
It sounds pretty good.

243
00:12:17,120 --> 00:12:19,720
Director, there's no breath mark in this song.

244
00:12:20,720 --> 00:12:23,120
Try sneaking a breath here.

245
00:12:56,240 --> 00:12:57,240
What are you laughing at?

246
00:12:57,240 --> 00:12:58,240
I'm not laughing.

247
00:13:00,400 --> 00:13:01,120
Say that again.

248
00:13:01,120 --> 00:13:02,800
Aren't you a thousand-year tree demon?

249
00:13:02,800 --> 00:13:04,200
Seems you're out of breath too.

250
00:13:04,200 --> 00:13:05,480
You think you got this?

251
00:13:06,480 --> 00:13:07,040
Come on.

252
00:13:07,040 --> 00:13:07,970
You give it a try.

253
00:13:08,560 --> 00:13:09,620
I didn't mean that.

254
00:13:09,920 --> 00:13:11,000
Come on.

255
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:11,920
Don't regret it.

256
00:13:11,920 --> 00:13:13,000
Scare me then.

257
00:13:14,720 --> 00:13:15,480
I'll show you how it's done.

258
00:13:15,480 --> 00:13:15,640
Come on.

259
00:13:15,640 --> 00:13:16,370
Show me then.

260
00:13:17,040 --> 00:13:17,640
Director.

261
00:13:52,480 --> 00:13:55,280
Director, she really doesn't have enough breath.

262
00:13:56,280 --> 00:13:59,120
And you claim to be the best female voice in our troupe.

263
00:13:59,120 --> 00:14:00,400
You are not up to it.

264
00:14:00,600 --> 00:14:01,240
Wait, when did I say

265
00:14:01,240 --> 00:14:02,320
I was the best female voice in the troupe?

266
00:14:02,320 --> 00:14:03,400
And how am I not up to it?

267
00:14:03,400 --> 00:14:03,880
Fine.

268
00:14:03,880 --> 00:14:06,080
Then from now on, I'm the best singer in the troupe.

269
00:14:06,080 --> 00:14:07,680
Can you stop being so sarcastic?

270
00:14:07,680 --> 00:14:08,920
How am I being sarcastic?

271
00:14:08,920 --> 00:14:09,880
Can you not be like this?

272
00:14:09,880 --> 00:14:11,200
Wait, how is that sarcastic?

273
00:14:11,200 --> 00:14:12,560
Wanru, just drop it.

274
00:14:13,080 --> 00:14:13,880
Meng Tejiao,

275
00:14:14,280 --> 00:14:15,120
whose side are you on?

276
00:14:15,120 --> 00:14:16,000
I'm not on anyone's side.

277
00:14:16,000 --> 00:14:17,440
I just want everyone to get along.

278
00:14:17,440 --> 00:14:18,600
No, we're not arguing.

279
00:14:18,600 --> 00:14:20,720
We are discussing a professional issue.

280
00:14:20,720 --> 00:14:21,400
Shut up.

281
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:23,800
If you want to argue, go outside.

282
00:14:24,040 --> 00:14:25,880
Come back to rehearse when you're done.

283
00:14:25,880 --> 00:14:28,680
If you argue until dark, we'll rehearse all night.

284
00:14:31,680 --> 00:14:32,280
Director,

285
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:33,680
I think

286
00:14:34,120 --> 00:14:36,050
it's not a matter of arguing or not.

287
00:14:36,120 --> 00:14:37,380
Even if they sing well,

288
00:14:38,040 --> 00:14:39,700
there will still be problems.

289
00:14:41,200 --> 00:14:42,200
Because this song

290
00:14:42,920 --> 00:14:44,320
just doesn't sound good.

291
00:14:53,480 --> 00:14:54,560
It's all your fault.

292
